# Line-ending policy.
#
# Without this file git applies its default text heuristic on checkout, which
# on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF. For most sources that is harmless. For a
# vendored artifact whose whole claim is "byte-identical to upstream" it is
# not: the Windows Test matrix caught three.module.min.js checking out at
# 677,941 bytes against the 677,935 recorded in vendor/PROVENANCE.json — six
# newlines, six extra bytes, and a SHA-256 that no longer matches upstream
# three.js r165.

# Default: let git normalise text in the repository, and check it out with
# native endings unless overridden below.
* text=auto

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendored third-party artifacts — never touch these bytes.
# Their SHA-256 is recorded in src/openlimno/fishtank/vendor/PROVENANCE.json
# and verified by tests/unit/test_vendor_provenance.py, which is what makes
# the provenance record meaningful rather than decorative.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
src/openlimno/fishtank/vendor/three.module.min.js -text
src/openlimno/fishtank/vendor/THREE_LICENSE      -text

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frozen test fixtures and reference data. Checksums and golden-file
# comparisons are taken over their exact bytes.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
*.parquet  -text
*.nc       -text
*.hdf      -text
*.zip      -text
*.png      -text

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Studio front-end assets. studio_assets.py inlines these into a page whose
# rendered SHA-256 is pinned by a test, and read_text() normalises newlines on
# read — so the page survives a CRLF checkout, but the files themselves must
# stay LF or the committed bytes differ per platform. Pinned explicitly rather
# than relying on the `text=auto` default.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
src/openlimno/*/assets/*.js   text eol=lf
src/openlimno/*/assets/*.mjs  text eol=lf
src/openlimno/*/assets/*.css  text eol=lf

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data and schema files read back by checksum-sensitive code paths.
# `openlimno reproduce` verifies SHA-256 over case inputs, so a CRLF
# checkout would break reproduction on Windows for a case authored on Linux.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
*.csv   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
